---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../lib/site';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Accessibility — Business Lab"
  description="Business Lab aims for WCAG 2.2 AA. What we do, what we know is not finished, and how to tell us about a barrier."
  path=""
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container column prose">
      <span class="eyebrow">Legal</span>
      <h1>Accessibility</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Business Lab is meant to work for everyone, on any phone, with a keyboard, a screen reader,
        larger text or no motion. This page says how far along that is and how to tell us when
        something gets in the way.
      </p>
      <p class="updated">Last updated {site.legalUpdated}.</p>

      <h2>Our target</h2>
      <p>
        We aim to meet the <a href="https://www.w3.org/TR/WCAG22/" rel="noopener noreferrer">Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG) 2.2</a>
        at level AA on every page. Until an independent audit has been done, the honest status is
        <strong>partially conformant</strong>: the parts we have checked pass, and we check more
        with every release.
      </p>

      <h2>What we do</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Body text is set in Atkinson Hyperlegible Next, a typeface designed for low-vision readers, at 18px or larger, and the layout survives 200% zoom.</li>
        <li>Every colour pair used for text meets at least 4.5:1 contrast. The site is light on every page; your browser's own dark or high-contrast mode works with it. The figures are published in our design documentation.</li>
        <li>Everything works with a keyboard alone, with a visible focus ring. Nothing fixed on the screen hides the focused element.</li>
        <li>Buttons, menus and lists of links have targets at least 44 pixels tall; a link inside a sentence is smaller, as WCAG allows, and every target is at least 24 by 24 pixels. Nothing is conveyed by colour alone.</li>
        <li>Animations are short, optional and switched off when your system asks for reduced motion.</li>
        <li>Calculators explain their results in a sentence, not only in a number, and every input has a visible label.</li>
        <li>Automated checks (axe-core) run on every page, on phone and desktop sizes, before any change is published, and the build fails on serious issues.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Known limitations</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Lessons are still being written; interactive lessons and charts will ship with text alternatives and data tables, and this list will name anything that falls short.</li>
        <li>Content is in English only for now. Hindi is planned for the India edition.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Tell us about a barrier</h2>
      <p>
        If something does not work for you, email{' '}
        <a href={`mailto:${site.contactEmail}`}>{site.contactEmail}</a> with the page address and
        what happened. We aim to reply within five days and to fix real barriers in the next
        release.
      </p>

      <h2>How this was assessed</h2>
      <p>
        Self-assessment against WCAG 2.2 AA using manual keyboard and screen-reader checks,
        contrast calculations for every token in the design system, and automated testing:
        axe-core via Playwright at 393px and 1280px, reflow checks at 320px, 360px and 640×400
        (200% zoom), forced colours and keyboard checks. Technologies relied on: HTML, CSS,
        JavaScript and WAI-ARIA.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
